WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/dashboard/components/RecentlyViewedWidget.tsx — a lightweight "back to where I was"
  dashboard surface:
    GlassPanel(p-4) → header[ Clock icon (cyan) + "Recently Viewed" (section-title) ]
                    → entries.length === 0
                        ? <p text-muted> "Pages you visit will appear here for quick access." </p>  (a
                          DELIBERATELY non-actionable hint — the "action" is the rest of the app; the web
                          audit-empty-state script forbids a cta-less EmptyState here, hence a plain <p>)
                        : <ul> entries.map → <li><Link to={entry.path}>[ iconForKind(kind) (cyan)
                                                  + title (truncate) + formatRelative(visited_at, now) ]</Link>
  Data: useRecentPages(limit=RECENT_PAGES_DISPLAY_LIMIT=5) — a SYNCHRONOUS, subscribe-on-change CLIENT-SIDE
        store (web/src/lib/recentPages.ts; getRecentPages + subscribeRecentPages), NOT an HTTP query. Plus
        useTranslation. formatRelative ladder: diff=max(0,now-visited); min=floor(diff/60000ms);
        <1→"Just now"; <60→"{min}m"; hr=floor(min/60)<24→"{hr}h"; else floor(hr/24)→"{day}d".
        iconForKind: vehicle→Car, drive→Route, charging→BatteryCharging, trip→Compass, geofence→MapPinned,
        year-review→CalendarDays, default(page)→FileText. classifyPath maps a stored path → kind + ref_id.
  Branches in the web leaf: exactly two — empty hint vs. populated list (the store read is synchronous,
  offline-first, and never throws/loads/goes-stale in the web). The native build adds the P4 states-contract
  chrome (loading / error / stale / offline) the prompt mandates, mapped faithfully to the local offline-first
  store — see STATES.

