STATES (every state renders — no hidden surfaces)
  loading  — model's pre-first-read phase → TSSkeleton rows (native chrome; before the first store snapshot).
  data     — entries present → navigable list (web <ul>).
  empty    — zero entries → the web's non-actionable hint <p> "Pages you visit will appear here…".
  error    — a corrupt/unreadable persisted store → QueryError-equivalent + Retry wired to model.refresh()
             (native chrome; the web store read is synchronous so the web leaf has no error branch).
  stale    — snapshot past the freshness window → "Stale" chip + cached-data banner + exactly-one guarded
             auto-refresh; the cached recents STAY VISIBLE.
  offline  — no connectivity → "Offline" chip + banner; the cached recents STAY VISIBLE (offline-first — the
             local store is the cached value the contract asks for).
  The loading/error/stale/offline overlays are the native P4 states-contract chrome the prompt mandates,
  mapped faithfully onto the offline-first local store (the same approach the predecessor feed surface
  AutomationActivityFeed uses). Every branch is reproduced + tested; none hides content.

